  "legend": [
    "Basic Quality Factors for Longitudinal Weld Joints in Pipes and Tubes, Ej (Cont'd)"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "GENERAL NOTES: (a) These weld joint quality factors, together with the referenced Notes, are requirements of this Code. (b) Notes marked with an asterisk (*) restate requirements found in the text of the Code. NOTES: (1) Specifications, except API, are ASTM. (2) *These quality factors are determined in accordance with para. 302.3.4(a). See para. 302.3.4(b) for enhancement of quality factors. See also para. 302.3.1(a), footnote 1. (3) *This specification includes requirements for random radiographic inspection for mill quality control. If the 0.90 weld joint quality factor is to be used, the welds shall meet the requirements of Table 341.3.2-1 for longitudinal butt welds with spot radiography in accordance with Table 302.3.4-1. This shall be a matter of special agreement between purchaser and manufacturer. (4) Not permitted for the P4 and P5 materials in Table 302.3.5-1 for Elevated Temperature Fluid Service. (5) This quality factor is also applicable for heavily cold-worked (HCW) ASTM A312 materials as defined in ASTM A312, para. 6.1.4."
  ],
